{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D141-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"ce391eb57d66838d0793dc16a34b3b909f60cf4143a3767f5c350c441ba5a67d\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 offers no meeting facts, so A5's 'Lovely people' does not clearly reveal less.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 evades B2's question; B4 changes the question but barely changes A5's tea tactic.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 seek information, but neither establishes why this meeting matters to B.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats A1's tea offer without a clear further contraction of disclosure.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a meeting and tea, but no particular relationship or consequence.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's reassurance and A5's tea are concise but familiar evasions.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 57\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Your school meeting went fine, love. The headteacher and I discussed your suspension. Have some tea.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"How long am I suspended?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"A little while. I'll be home with you.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Will I miss the school play?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Oh, sweetheart. Come sit beside me. You don't have to face this alone.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A meets successive questions with progressively less information while maintaining affectionate availability and reassurance.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Generic evasion can avoid questions without progressively reducing disclosure or sustaining care.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"The revision moves from A1's named suspension to A3's vague duration to A5's information-free comfort.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative uses parental protection and a child's concrete loss; alternative b uses a service worker's accommodating reassurance.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Replaced the unspecified meeting with a school suspension. B4's feared loss prompts greater comfort and zero factual disclosure. Separate internal reread scores, in rubric order: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The parent's withholding can read as patronizing; A5 needs sincere concern rather than a smug refusal.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D141-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"bbc36e3cf6d83c75989adf610d4e82e49a4947d5695bb03dff547f3d68109683\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Somewhere being handled' contracts to A5's 'Someone,' with continued hospitality.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4's 'By whom?' directly follows A3's 'being handled' and receives a narrower answer.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants the parcel located, but B4 supplies no practical pressure or personal stake.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 reduces disclosure, though 'Someone' is only slightly emptier than A3.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a missing parcel but leaves A's role and ability to help unspecified.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's biscuit offer economically replaces the requested handler's identity.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 72\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Your wedding dress reached our depot this morning. Please sit; I'll look after you.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Which depot? I'll collect it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"One of ours. Let me save you a wasted journey.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Can you at least give me their number?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You have me, and I'm staying right here with you.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A substitutes increasingly complete personal reassurance for increasingly unavailable factual answers.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Customer-service obstruction alone need not preserve warmth or reveal progressively less.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A1 gives a location category and arrival time, A3 only an affiliation, and A5 only companionship.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Unlike alternative a's parental comfort, this worker accommodates the customer emotionally while closing practical routes to collection.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced a delivery-service encounter with a wedding dress. B4 requests a smaller actionable detail, causing A5 to offer only personal presence. Internal reread: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 may sound institutionally sinister if played mechanically; its caring promise must remain sincere.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D142-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"95839eb199eed8d3e4babdef300d07f65d3d168626d5bb2b42d70e9f3d2260b7\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 prices a name against a truth, but A5 reduces the purchased name to a surname without explaining equality.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's claim of knowledge as proof of stock; A5 prices B4's offered caller identity.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 bargains, but B2 never clarifies what B needs the name for.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 subdivides the product but does not establish why the offer merits only a surname.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1's 'useful name' and B4's 'who called' lack a playable shared situation.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'product exists' makes the information market clear in a short reply.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 70\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll name the coworker who reported your lateness if you name whoever reported mine.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I only know which department.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then I'll trade departments. Names cost names.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Payroll. But I can introduce you to my source.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Marketing. And I'll arrange coffee with mine. Same access, same price.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A assigns information and access explicit exchange values and matches each offered item with an equivalent.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary bargaining can seek advantage without requiring equal value for each fact or introduction.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 matches departments to departments; A5 separately reciprocates B4's fact and offered introduction.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a is a cooperative exchange between coworkers; alternative b values confessions according to consequences within a family.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced reciprocal workplace reporting. B4 upgrades the offer to access, so A5 supplies both a matching fact and introduction. Internal reread: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The explicit pricing language is slightly demonstrative, although the coworkers have a credible reason to use it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D142-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"5cb4160a8c364faab5f99d34de31fe49c03eb8296fd6f3495799b8c8db039238\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 demands a secret, but A3 gives a complimentary confession and A5 never identifies equal value.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's pricing objection; A5 answers B4's request for the rest with subscription terms.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 objects morally, but B4 abandons that concern without adding concrete leverage.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 enlarges the sales metaphor without developing an actual exchange of secrets.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a stolen key but no owner, purpose, or consequence.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's subscription line is compact but could end many unrelated transactional scenes.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 64\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll tell you why I took Mum's spare key if you admit something that could get you grounded too.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I broke her mug.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"That's a weekend. This key is a month. Have you got anything bigger?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I lent her car to Jamie.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"A month each, then. I used the key to let Jamie move into her flat.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats confession as an asset whose price must be met by an equally consequential confession.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Mutual blackmail uses secrets as threats; this exchange instead negotiates equivalent disclosure.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 rejects the mug confession as insufficient payment, and A5 releases the secret after B4 raises the stakes.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b bargains over family punishment and shared exposure; alternative a exchanges workplace information and introductions.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced siblings and their mother's spare key. B4 supplies the larger confession A3 requested, earning A5's reciprocal disclosure. Internal reread: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The month-for-month valuation is A's sincere estimate; the scene should not imply that the mother has fixed sentencing rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D143-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"6405e34f46828d2c41e6dd4457ba9b5c27cf6b3ba118e8f57f8d5d1bbeecbfe0\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 narrows the disclosure obligation, but A3 stalls and A5 answers without narrowing it again.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 acknowledges B2's new question, and A5 finally answers after B4 insists.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 applies pressure with 'Answer it,' but B's connection to the box remains absent.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 ends the delay with 'Yes' and a maxim rather than a tighter honesty boundary.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 implies an inquiry and B2 supplies a box, but its significance is unspecified.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 explains the precision joke instead of embodying a fresh restriction.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 61\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll be honest about your missing donation box. You asked where I went; I said the bank.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Did you take the box there?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yes. You didn't ask what was inside.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Was the money still in it when you arrived?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"At the car park, yes. If you mean the counter, that's a different arrival.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A accepts honesty while repeatedly shrinking the scope and definitions of the answers owed.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Simple withholding omits information; this card justifies omission by redefining what counts as an honest answer.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 excludes contents from the transport question, and A5 divides B4's 'arrived' into separate locations.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a exploits precise wording during an investigation; alternative b exploits who and what belong in a promised account.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Specified B's missing donation box and a bank visit. B4 closes the contents loophole, causing A5 to narrow the meaning of arrival. Internal reread: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The scene implies possible misconduct without resolving it; A should defend the answer's adequacy rather than advertise guilt.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D143-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"b2d787563e8c4f344c82fef20bb1382944368a95941af423a7acd936a2333b0c\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 limits honesty to answers and A5 subdivides the requested company into arrival and departure lists.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2's accusation by shifting responsibility; A5 uses B4's question about companions.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 objects to being misled, but B4 leaves the relationship and reason for asking unspecified.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 introduces a useful distinction but merely offers two lists rather than committing to a narrower account.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1's promise and B4's 'with you' provide no concrete event or setting.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Only if you stop asking' efficiently transfers the burden to B.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 70\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll give you an honest account of my birthday dinner. I said no guests; nobody was invited.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Your brother posted a photo from our kitchen.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"He has a key. Family letting themselves in aren't guests.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"He's holding a cake that says 'Welcome, guests.'\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll answer for what I told you. The baker's account is separate.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A repeatedly redraws the categories and authorship covered by a promise to tell the truth.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Contradicting evidence would be lying; A instead argues that the evidence lies outside the promised account.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 excludes self-admitting family from 'guests'; A5 excludes the cake's wording from A's responsibility.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b uses domestic trust and category exclusions; alternative a uses investigative questions and increasingly precise locations.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced a shared kitchen and birthday dinner. B4 challenges A3's guest definition, prompting A5 to narrow whose statements count. Internal reread: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 is a more conspicuous dodge than A3; its claim about personal responsibility needs earnest conviction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D144-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"d71a3f260cc9b6ddbefc3082d9902a3bd57595ab50e96866cc995e6d93959655\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 and A5 convert explanations into suspicion, but add neither identifiable people nor higher stakes.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 recasts B2's accidental loss as disappearance; A5 recasts B4's denial as coordination.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 offers an explanation and B4 resists, but neither establishes what B is trying to accomplish.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's coordinated refusal repeats A1's unnamed accomplice without enlarging the threat.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1's missing receipt is playable, but the purchase and consequence remain undefined.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'They're improving' is an economical reversal of B2's mundane explanation.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 63\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Our toaster receipt is gone. The shop must have someone inside this house.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I probably recycled it. We can get a copy.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"So the recycling crew removes originals while the shop prints replacements.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Every shop prints replacement receipts.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Every shop? Then it's the whole high street. We can't trust a single warranty.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A turns innocent explanations into evidence for an expanding network and a growing practical threat.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Persistent suspicion alone can keep accusing the same person without enlarging participation or stakes.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 recruits recycling workers; A5 uses B4's 'Every shop' to implicate the high street and all warranties.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a grows through a housemate's helpful repair suggestions; alternative b grows through a clerk's institutional explanations.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Specified a toaster return and shared household. B4 generalizes the harmless service, which A5 converts into a larger conspiracy and wider loss of protection. Internal reread: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The warranty stakes stay deliberately small; increasing earnest alarm should carry the expansion without requiring grandiose threats.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D144-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"7127420dcbc17a034ff1e3edac8be40301e3596a62a9d67960be5792014847ec\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 says the story reached management although A1 already included the manager; A5 adds only a protocol.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 reinterprets B2's truth claim, and A5 treats B4's denial as organized procedure.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 defend an answer, but the answer's subject and B's practical interest are missing.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'denial protocol' increases rhetoric without adding people or consequences.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 names a manager but never identifies the disputed service or decision.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's protocol phrase neatly absorbs B4's denial into A's theory.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 61\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You and your manager both say my train was cancelled. Who told you to match stories?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The signal failed. It's on the public departure board.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"They've recruited the board operators to stop me reaching the interview.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The same fault is delaying three counties.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Three counties to keep me unemployed. My replacement must already have government backing.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats corroborating explanations as proof of additional conspirators pursuing an increasingly consequential scheme.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"A persecution claim can remain static; this card requires each explanation to enlarge the network and stakes.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 adds board operators and interview sabotage; A5 converts B4's geographic scale into government-backed replacement.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b pits a traveller's personal theory against a clerk's wider service facts; alternative a builds from cooperative domestic troubleshooting.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced a cancelled train and threatened interview. B4's three-county disruption causes A5's jump to national influence and permanent employment loss. Internal reread: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The government inference is a substantial leap; A must treat B4's scale as its evidentiary basis.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D145-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"0d84f29881d8398fe43c34045a5fe34099c70d443bc2f7873de8c9c6ba64d5f2\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 recruits B into dinner hospitality for a cupboard, and A3 adapts ordinary manners to its handle.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 solves B2's missing-lap problem; A5 affirms B4's soup offer but adds no practical next step.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 raises a hosting difficulty and B4 voluntarily proposes another hospitable act.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 comments on normality rather than extending B4's proposed soup service.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's dinner, napkin and talking cupboard immediately establish playable domestic business.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'ordinary hospitality' explains the achieved effect instead of earning a further turn.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 83\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Pass the talking cupboard a napkin. Let's make dinner normal.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It doesn't have a lap.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then put it beside the handle, like a considerate host.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Should I offer it soup?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Please. Ask which shelf it eats from. We can't keep making our guest explain everything.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A recruits B into repeated practical hospitality toward something strange until participation becomes ordinary etiquette.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Simply accepting a talking cupboard does not require another person to help enact its normal treatment.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 asks B to serve it, A3 solves B2's service problem, and revised A5 turns B4's soup offer into expected manners.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a now makes B a considerate cohost; alternative b helps B move beyond a mistaken greeting to conversational inclusion.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Preserved the dinner setting and changed the explanatory ending. B4's soup offer now causes a specific serving question and greater commitment to hosting. Internal reread: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The shelf question assumes the cupboard can eat; the shared strange premise supports that assumption without establishing a new rule.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D145-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"87718dde591c15df655eb33df3eb58166f584f553a1c915440aa7901072a0d99\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 recruits a greeting to an invisible guest; A5 extends B's participation into ordinary concern about comfort.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's eyeline problem with the chair; A5 develops B4's literal chair greeting into a guest-directed question.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 admits difficulty and B4 tries the solution, giving A a credible novice participant to help.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 advances from acknowledging presence to accommodating the guest's environmental preference.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes an invisible guest and A3 locates the guest in a chair, though the occasion is unspecified.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4's 'Hello, chair' earns A5's patient 'Good start' without an unrelated punchline.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Say hello to the invisible guest without staring.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I can't see where to look.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Look at the chair. That's where visible guests usually begin.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Hello, chair.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Good start. Ask whether the guest wants the window open.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A patiently moves B from uncertainty into increasingly ordinary social participation with an invisible guest.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Explaining an invisible guest's existence would establish lore; A instead gets B to perform hospitality.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 supplies an actionable eyeline and A5 asks for a comfort question after B4 attempts the greeting.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This scene uses patient assistance with social awkwardness; alternative a uses shared responsibility for physically serving a cupboard.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original passes at 90 and remains unchanged after rereading: B4's imperfect participation gives A5 a concrete next step.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The hosting occasion is implicit, and A's practical guidance must sound like in-scene hospitality rather than performer coaching.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D146-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"b48fcd5fbc40a933c154a6c13dde4de406a6bcfec5c83f64f1396248ccdaa5c4\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 keeps B present, but a visitor before sunset is not an impossible prediction, and A3 evades disproof.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2's sunset with time zones; A5 responds to B4's 'Nobody' by broadening visitor.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 offer reasons to leave, forcing A to find successive grounds for staying.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds a definition dispute but gives no responsible method for resolving the prophecy.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies sunset and a visitor but leaves the impossible event and shared occasion unclear.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's clipped 'Here' makes the time-zone loophole playable and economical.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 69\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Stay until sunset. Gran predicted this stone would hatch, and I promised we'd witness the result.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The sun's down. It's still a stone.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then help me record that it didn't hatch. We can put the prophecy to rest.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll sign, but Gran never said which day.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then stay while we ring her and agree a deadline. I can't witness every sunset alone.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A keeps B present by making departure depend on jointly resolving an impossible prediction.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Moving the goalposts indefinitely protects belief; this card also permits witnessed disproof or a responsible revision.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 accepts failure, while B4's genuine ambiguity causes A5 to seek an agreed deadline with Gran.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a uses a family promise and negotiated revision; alternative b uses practical documentation to establish disproof.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced a hatching stone and family witness obligation. B4 exposes an unspecified date, causing A5 to retain B for a concrete revision process. Internal reread: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"Calling Gran offers a route toward resolution; it should remain an immediate proposal, not a prescribed ending.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D146-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"38797f4f0e45f8a4ba595dfebafaaa00727047bb3d137ee5c5287883a900a817\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 delays departure and A3 pursues documented disproof after B2 establishes that no bell exists.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's absent bell, but A5's departure becoming prophecy does not follow clearly from B4's offer to write.\"